'''''Dojo nabe''''' (Japanese: 泥鰌鍋 or ドジョウ鍋; dojō nabe) is a Japanese ''[[nabemono]]'' dish.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://web-japan.org/nipponia/nipponia41/en/appetit/appetit01.html|title=Dojo : Bon Appetit! : NIPPONIA No. 41|website=web-japan.org}}</ref> To prepare the dish, [[pond loach]]es are cooked in a [[hot pot]]. The freshwater fishes are either killed ahead of cooking or are first soaked in cold sake and then cooked alive.{{cn|date=November 2017}}
